# Trivy vulnerability suppressions.
# Each entry MUST document why the advisory does not apply and be re-checked
# whenever dependencies change. Trivy reads this file from the repo root, so it
# is honored by both the CI scans (docker-publish, cve-trivy-scan) and local runs.

# Every entry carries an exp: date so it lapses and must be re-reviewed instead
# of silently hiding a future advisory.

# GO-2026-5932: golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp is unmaintained / unsafe by design.
# Re-verified 2026-09-24 with x/crypto v0.57.0 (v0.5.0 image):
#   - `go list -deps ./cmd/goeland-server` reports zero openpgp packages;
#   - `make vuln-check` (govulncheck, symbol level) reports the code is not affected;
#   - x/crypto only arrives via go-cloud-k8s-common-libs -> Echo -> x/crypto/acme.
# Trivy flags this module-level advisory from the x/crypto version in the binary's
# build metadata, not from reachable code. UNKNOWN severity, no fix available.
GO-2026-5932 exp:2026-12-31
